@startuml 02-containers

!pragma layout smetana lefttoright

title FlowAI Platform - Task flow (runtime slice)

package "Automation layer" {
    [Webhook Handler] as wh
    [Jira Poller] as jira
    [GitLab Handler] as gl
}

package "Core" {
    [API Gateway] as gw
    [Event Router] as er
    database "Event Router DB" as erdb
    database "Secret Service" as sec
}

package "Executor fleet (multi-cluster)" {
    [Executor A (k8s-A)] as exA
    [Executor B (k8s-B)] as exB
    [Executor local (Docker)] as exL
}

wh --> er : REST POST /tasks (event)
jira --> er : REST POST /tasks (event)
gl --> er : REST POST /tasks (event)

' GW is an auth-aware reverse proxy.
' It only does: (1) validate auth, (2) route to a backend service,
' (3) return the backend's response. No business logic, no state, no writes.
gw --> er : REST proxy (UI -> /state, /tasks, /control, /subscribe, ...)
gw --> sec : REST proxy (UI -> /secrets)
gw <-- er : REST/WS push (live events, relayed to UI WS)

er --> erdb : read/write tasks + events (sole owner)
er --> sec : REST open env (validate secret_ids, fetch env at dispatch)
er --> exA : REST POST task_spec + scope_token (dispatch)
er --> exB : REST POST task_spec + scope_token (dispatch)
er --> exL : REST POST task_spec + scope_token (dispatch)
er <-- exA : REST POST event (live)
er <-- exB : REST POST event (live)
er <-- exL : REST POST event (live)

exA --> sec : REST open env (at task start, inject into container)
exB --> sec : REST open env (at task start)
exL --> sec : REST open env (at task start)

note right of gw
  Auth-aware reverse proxy.
  Only logic: validate auth, route to
  backend service, return response.
  NO business logic.
  NO state of its own.
  NO writes.
  Holds WS connections for UI and
  relays live events from ER.
end note

note right of er
  Backend service.
  Sole owner of ER DB.
  Replaces queues: tasks and events
  live in the ER DB.
  Receives task submissions from automation
  and proxied requests from UI (via GW).
  Dispatches tasks to executors via REST.
  Receives live events from executors.
  Pushes live events to subscribers (GW).
  Does NOT modify message content.
  Sends REST queries to SS (open env).
end note

note right of sec
  Backend service.
  Two surfaces:
  store (write) - called by GW (proxying UI)
  open env (read) - called by ER and EX
  (GW does NOT call open env anymore -
  it has no business logic)
end note

@enduml